{"course":{"id":"s18","title":"Atomic – Cambridge Lower Secondary Mathematics — Stage 8","units":[{"n":1,"t":"Integers"},{"n":2,"t":"Expressions, Formulae and Equations"},{"n":3,"t":"Place Value and Rounding"},{"n":4,"t":"Decimals"},{"n":5,"t":"Angles and Constructions"},{"n":6,"t":"Collecting Data"},{"n":7,"t":"Fractions"},{"n":8,"t":"Shapes and Symmetry"},{"n":9,"t":"Sequences and Functions"},{"n":10,"t":"Percentages"},{"n":11,"t":"Graphs"},{"n":12,"t":"Ratio and Proportion"},{"n":13,"t":"Probability"},{"n":14,"t":"Position and Transformation"},{"n":15,"t":"Distance, Area and Volume"},{"n":16,"t":"Interpreting and Discussing Results"}]},"unit":{"n":3,"stage":18,"title":"Place Value and Rounding","strandShort":"Number","blurb":"Multiplying and dividing by 0.1 and 0.01, and rounding to decimal places and significant figures.","strand":"Number","framework":"Cambridge Lower Secondary Mathematics (0862), Stage 8","lesson":true,"subject":"maths","read":"media/read/m8u03.pdf"},"objectives":{"O1":{"code":"8Np.01","sec":"3.1","codeNote":"","t":"Multiply and divide integers and decimals by 0.1 and 0.01, and explain the effect."},"O2":{"code":"8Np.02","sec":"3.2","codeNote":"","t":"Round numbers to a given number of decimal places or significant figures."}},"sections":[{"id":"3.1","title":"Multiplying and dividing by 0.1 and 0.01","objs":["O1"],"lesson":[{"k":"idea","t":"Equivalent operations","p":["Multiplying by **0.1** is the same as **dividing by 10**. Multiplying by **0.01** is the same as **dividing by 100**.","Dividing by **0.1** is the same as **multiplying by 10**. Dividing by **0.01** is the same as **multiplying by 100**."],"table":{"head":["Operation","Same as"],"rows":[["× 0.1","÷ 10"],["× 0.01","÷ 100"],["÷ 0.1","× 10"],["÷ 0.01","× 100"]]}},{"k":"example","t":"Using place value","p":[],"q":"Work out 36 × 0.01 and 4.2 ÷ 0.1.","steps":[["36 × 0.01 = 36 ÷ 100 = 0.36","digits move 2 places right"],["4.2 ÷ 0.1 = 4.2 × 10 = 42","digits move 1 place left"]],"a":"0.36